1
00:05:25,714 --> 00:05:31,714
For Steve, his adventure isn't all black and white.

2
00:10:51,428 --> 00:10:57,428
Penguins is a documentary, family film directed by Alastair Fothergill.

3
00:16:17,142 --> 00:16:23,142
The story of Steve, an Adélie penguin, on a quest to
find a life partner and start a family.

4
00:21:42,857 --> 00:21:48,857
When Steve meets with Wuzzo the emperor penguin they become friends.

5
00:27:08,571 --> 00:27:14,571
But nothing comes easy in the icy Antarctic.

6
00:32:34,285 --> 00:32:40,285
Narrator (voice), played by Ed Helms.

7
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Penguins is a 2019 American nature documentary film
directed by Alastair Fothergill and Jeff Wilson.

8
00:43:25,714 --> 00:43:31,714
The coming-of-age story follows an Adélie penguin named Steve, who joins fellow males in the icy
Antarctic spring on a quest to build a suitable nest, find a life partner and start a family.

9
00:48:51,428 --> 00:48:57,428
The American release of the film is narrated by Ed Helms.

10
00:54:17,142 --> 00:54:23,142
Produced by Disneynature, the film was released in the United States on April 17, 2019, five days before Earth
Day and four years to the day of the release of fellow Disneynature production Monkey Kingdom.

11
00:59:42,857 --> 00:59:48,857
It is the thirteenth nature documentary to be
released under the Disneynature label.

12
01:05:08,571 --> 01:05:14,571
The film received positive reviews from critics, who
singled out the "beautiful cinematography".

13
01:10:34,285 --> 01:10:40,285
The film explores themes of penguin, wildlife,
antarctica, life challenges, mating ritual.
